&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to build the event-processing pipelines and services that turn Nebius product usage into revenue.&lt;br&gt;You will work on systems that process a continuous stream of usage events, where correctness and failure recovery matter as much as throughput. The output is money: a silently dropped or double-counted event is a real financial error.&lt;br&gt;Usage of every Nebius product arrives as a stream of events. Our pipelines and services ingest, validate, enrich and price it in near real time, and deliver the results to invoicing, reporting and customer-facing account management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build stateful streaming pipelines that compute billed consumption in near real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and operate Go services that ingest usage events, move data between our storage systems and deliver consumption data to users through usage APIs and billing data exports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guarantee correctness under failures: idempotency, exactly-once processing and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate transactional storage, persistent queues and change data capture under high throughput.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable streaming infrastructure rather than solving each use case independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, scalability, latency and observability of the billing platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of your systems: design, implementation, reliability and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience building and operating backend, streaming or data-intensive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to reason about consistency and data correctness under failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with databases, messaging systems or event-processing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to investigate unfamiliar systems and solve problems without an obvious predefined solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability and willingness to learn the team&#39;s technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a stateful stream-processing framework such as Apache Flink or Kafka Streams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing streaming pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating services in Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Technology stack&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go, Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apache Flink&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;YDB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;YTsaurus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Messaging and event-streaming systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
